Z||000000||MooCow||09-27-2000||09:21 PM||||Okay when I turn the wheel slitly is makes a squuking noise from the tires.  No it isn't the tires squlling becasue im taking corners to fast.  So is it my beerings or is it my bakes or rotors or calibers because I have no idea at all about any of thoses things.  Please let me know.<P>                              Thanks Ken||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||09-27-2000||11:42 PM||||I have a beering problem to... I'm out of it.<P>Make a big turn, drive in a circle, and GENTLELY tap the brakes enough to tighten the calipers and let off the pedal. If the noise stops with very little pressure it's likely a pad dragging. There isn't always an easy answer if that's the case. <P>A loose/worn bearing can also cause it. If there's a little play in them the rotor can move and drag a pad. You can usually see allot of play but it only takes a little to drag a pad.<P>the tugging of the brake line can cause this even if everything is working perfect otherwise. Those rubber lines are pretty stiff and can put a good tug on the caliper. You might could rework the line a bit if that's what's the cause.<P>If the noise DOES NOT stop when you tap the pedal check all the rotor shields. You may have one bent toward the rotor. take all the wheels off and inspect each sheild for marks where the edge of the rotor hit it.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 09-28-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||MooCow||09-29-2000||06:29 AM||||Okay I went in a circle and it squicked until I slightly pressed the brakes then went away until I stopped puching them.  I thne took the wheels of and tried to rotate the wheels and they rub.  Now is this bearings or do you think brake bads and rotors need to be turned.  If it is brake pads then should I wait till next year to do or can I do it now and it will still work fine after sitting all winter under a car cover and a tarp in the back yard?????????<P>                         Thanks Ken||||reg||5
Z||000003||theogre||09-29-2000||09:28 AM||||If you are going to leave it sit that long you may as well wait until next year. You're just going to rust up the rotors and have to fool with them again if you did the brakes now.<P><p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 09-29-2000).]||||reg||1
